# Chip Measurement — Phase A: Crashlytics (PERIPHERY)
#
# ACCEPTANCE CONTRACT (written before Phase A implementation edits)
# A1 GIVEN Firebase config succeeds and the separately committed app-target
#    dependencies are present, WHEN the app launches, THEN Crashlytics initializes
#    alongside Firebase without changing the visible launch flow.
# A2 GIVEN assessment persistence fails, WHEN AssessmentCoordinator swallows the
#    failure and continues task generation, THEN Crashlytics records the same error
#    and the existing saveError/continuation behavior is unchanged.
# A3 GIVEN identity migration persistence fails, WHEN IdentityService preserves its
#    best-effort return behavior, THEN Crashlytics records the write failure and the
#    built identity is still returned.
# A4 GIVEN workflow submission fails, WHEN WorkflowService propagates the error to
#    its existing caller behavior, THEN Crashlytics records the error exactly once at
#    the shared service boundary and still throws the original error.
# A5 GIVEN a temporary DEBUG-only forced-crash trigger, WHEN the installed simulator
#    app crashes outside the debugger and relaunches, THEN Crashlytics console or API
#    evidence proves receipt; the trigger is removed before commit.
# A6 GIVEN the final Phase A diff, WHEN grep checks, the exact iPhone 17 Pro build,
#    fresh-context validation, and diff review run, THEN A1-A5 receive an
#    evidence-backed PASS/FAIL; no deployment occurs and project.pbxproj remains
#    unchanged from prerequisite commit bf3af26.
#
# NEEDS-CLARIFICATION (bounded, reversible interpretations)
# - WorkflowService has no swallowed catch of its own. The shared service boundary
#   records and rethrows so every caller retains its current behavior without editing
#   multiple views or double-reporting a single submission failure.
# - Identity migration's `try?` write is converted to do/catch solely to expose the
#   same swallowed error to Crashlytics; its nil/success return contract is unchanged.
